A||||13||JohnnyK||Can't defrag harddrive?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-09-2001||01:23 AM||||I'm tryin to defrag my hard drive, and ever 10 seconds or so it says "Hard Drive contents changed. Restarting" so I control alt-del'd and closed all the programs that are running except for explorer, and it still does that?! Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-09-2001||01:32 AM||||Had the same problem recently.message said"Some application or windows itself is writing to the area of hard drive being defragged. Defrag has started over x-times. please exit this program and close any open applications that may be running then try again" or something like that. Turned out to be my anti-virus was trying to make backup or Zone Alarm firewall. I had to turn both of them completely off and temporarily remove them from the start-up group, then restart and run defrag. good luck<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRiAD||08-09-2001||01:54 AM||||Wow...this is funny (not your problem, but that I had the same one FOR OVER 2 YEARS!<P>Hehe, I <I>think</I> I solved it tonight...<P>I killed the MS Office Toolbar...completely. <BR>I had to also kill "Real" player to be able to defrag. <P>My PC is loving me for the first time in YEARS...literally!<P>Man, I KNEW that toolbar was trouble!<P>Hope this helps!||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||08-09-2001||02:14 AM||||since you mentioned it I might have taken everything out of my startup grp including real player and my earthlink toolbar. Wonder what a tol bar has to do with defrag?||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||08-09-2001||02:19 AM||||Mine did that as well.  <P>I'm using Norton System Works 200x now.  <P>If I recall, I believe a prompt comes up asking you in est if you want to ignore that message in the future.  Are you selecting yes if it does?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||mrgone||08-09-2001||02:35 AM||||do a crtl-alt-del and close any of the programs you have running in the background. only the nesseitiys(sp) :P should be there<P>(too bad ya cant play mp3s and defrag, eh?)||||reg||1
Z||000006||maryjane||08-09-2001||02:43 AM||||When it asked if I wanted to ignore the error message in the future, I clicked yes. It went ahead and defragged, but was slower than hades.(Thought it was past your bedtime J. You can send the Beanie files when you want to)<BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||08-09-2001||02:50 AM||||This is a common prob...heres what you do...<BR>Turn off your computer and then restart it in "safe mode"..this is done by either holding down the left "control" key while the computer is booting up, or, (more commonly), holding down the...I believe, the F9 key while the computer is booting up...(its one of the "F" keys..I think its F9)..keep holding it down until you get a black screen w the options listed (that you normally dont get)..."safe mode" is # 3.<BR>When the computer boots in safe mode, your desktop will look strange..dont worry, its supposed to. Then you can defrag w/ no worries.<BR>(I read it in a computer mag awhile back, and its the only way I can defrag). Good luck, M7F||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||08-09-2001||03:38 AM||||Thanks man! I never really thought about Safe Mode for defragging (I think it's f8 btw). I'll give that a try in the morning.||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||08-09-2001||07:41 AM||||Yeah thats a known problem with defrag, safe mode is the best way around the problem.||||reg||14
Z||000010||JSocha||08-09-2001||09:38 AM||||Don't know if it was the system, but just in case:<P>Be careful if they are IBM drives.  I have ended up hosing two of my drives (in the same computer) doing it that way.  Quit buying IBM drives after that and haven't tried that way since, so I don't know if was my system or just the drives.  Not going to try and find out either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> . F8 is the key though.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000011||Raydar||08-09-2001||09:51 AM||||I used to kill everything that was running in the system tray, in order to defrag.<BR>I like the "safe mode" idea better, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000012||JohnnyK||08-09-2001||03:43 PM||||Thats the thing though, i DID kill everything, and it still wouldn't work. Makes me believe there is something sneaky going on in the background.||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||08-09-2001||08:43 PM||||there's an easy solution to this that works in all but a few cases.... restart the machine into safe mode and run defrag.||||reg||1
